  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 512 PM MDT Fri Aug 14 2026/ \n\n- Meteorological Overview: \n\nMoist, southwest flow aloft and overall north-to-east low level flow \nwill help to maintain precipitation chances and below-to-near normal \ntemperatures through the middle of the upcoming work. Over this \nstretch Sunday and Monday will be the closest to normal, with \nrespect to high temperatures, as surface winds briefly become \nsouthwesterly and supporting some \"warming\" as compared to the \nSaturday, Tuesday, and Wednesday. Monsoonal moisture lifting north \nand east within the southwest flow aloft will maintain daily chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms, most notably from Monday \nafternoon/evening through the Tuesday afternoon. While thunderstorms \nfrom this weekend through the middle of the work week will generally \nbe of the garden variety a few stronger storms producing strong \nwind gusts can't be ruled out as low level moisture gradually \nerodes leading to inverted-V soundings, especially across \nSouthwest Montana. - Moldan\n\n- Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nFlooding risk through this evening: \n\n\n12z Hi-Res Ensemble Forecast (HREF) guidance supports a 20-30% \nchance that hourly rainfall rates could exceed 0.25\"/hr from the \nlate afternoon through evening hours tonight over the burn scars \nacross the Pioneer Mountains, with these probabilities appearing \nreasonable given morning observations of between 0.1\"-0.3\" across \nSouthwest through North Central Montana. Given that the threshold \nfor flash flooding is so low over the active fires in the Pioneers, \nand that they have already received a wetting rain over the previous \n24 hours, a Flash Flood Watch remains in effect through 9 pm this \nevening.\n\nConcerns for flash flooding on the the Horse Gulch Burn Scar remain \nlower than that of the Pioneer Mountain Burn Scars given a lower \nprobability for hourly rainfall rates to exceed 0.5\"/hr here, with \nthese probabilities being around a 10% chance. While flash flooding \ncan not be ruled across the Horse Gulch Burn Scar through the \nevening hours tonight confidence in any flooding remains too low to \nissue a Flash Food Watch. -Moldan/AM",
